# Python bytecode + tool caches produced by the Track SANDBOX test harness (mirrors
# backend/.gitignore). The harness runs under the backend uv env; these are never committed.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# A stray `uv.lock` written here by a `uv` invocation that resolved its project root to
# `sandbox/` rather than `backend/`. The supervisor has no project of its own — it runs under
# the backend env — so a lockfile at this level is always an accident, and committing one would
# pin the supervisor's deps somewhere nobody looks. Same reasoning as the package-lock anchor
# below: keep an accidental lockfile out of a tree whose real lockfile is build-critical.
uv.lock
# ...and the `.venv/` the same stray invocation creates. Root cause now REMOVED: the
# `[project]`-less `pyproject.toml` that made uv read this directory as a virtual workspace
# root (astral-sh/uv#4541) is gone, replaced by `pytest.ini` + `ruff.toml`, which uv ignores.
# Both entries are kept as belt-and-braces against anyone reintroducing a pyproject here.
.venv/

# Tool caches
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Node install artifacts anywhere under this tree — never committed. Untracked so they can
# never shadow the tracked, build-critical template/package-lock.json (Dockerfile.sandbox's
# `npm ci` depends on it).
node_modules/

# Tool output from the seed workspace (`seed/`), which exists only to VERIFY the golden
# template's reference file: `seed/flight-data.ts` is typechecked under the template's own
# `strict` settings and unit-tested there, then rendered into
# `template/lib/flight-data.reference.ts` by `seed/generate-reference.mjs`. Nothing in `seed/`
# ships — `Dockerfile.sandbox` never copies or installs it — so nothing it produces is committed.
# Its install is already covered by `node_modules/` above; these are what tsc and vitest leave.
#
# `seed/package-lock.json` is deliberately NOT here. It is tracked, because "verified under
# strict" is a claim about a specific resolution of four packages, and a year from now that claim
# is only reproducible from a lockfile (`npm ci`), not from four pinned direct versions whose
# transitive tree has moved on.
seed/coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
